SUMMARY:Kolam: Indian House Decorating
DESCRIPTION:“Kolam” is a traditional form of Indian folk art\, originally created as decorative patterns drawn at the entrance of homes. These intricate designs were intended to form a symbolic maze that would trap evil spirits and prevent them from entering the house.In this art and craft activity\, visitors will have the opportunity to experience and create Kolam patterns firsthand. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Community Partner:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKalabharathi School of Dance is a premier dance institution and performance company dedicated to preserving and sharing the traditions of Bharatanatyam. Celebrating 29 years in Oregon\, it is an approved center for Bharatanatyam certification through APAA\, India. \n\n\n\nWith over 100 students\, Kalabharathi is known for its award-winning productions\, community collaborations\, and performances across Oregon and Washington. The school has also presented more than 29 Arangetrams over the past 15 years\, supporting students in reaching important milestones in their artistic journey. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/kolam-indian-house-decorating/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:AANHPI Heritage Month
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/Picture2-7.webp
END:VEVENT
