SUMMARY:Music in The Garden
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy the gentle sounds of live Chinese music on traditional instruments such as erhu\, ruan qin\, and pipa. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNoon – 3 PM | Fridays\, April 24 – September 25\, 2026 \n\n\n\nAs you stroll the garden pathways\, enjoy traditional Chinese music of erhu or guzheng by Lan Su musicians.  \n\n\n\nThe erhu is a bowed\, two-stringed Chinese vertical musical instrument. The guzheng is a traditional Chinese stringed instrument with 21 strings and movable bridges. \n\n\n\n\nGet Admission\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/live-chinese-music-in-the-garden/2026-05-22/
